{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1450754-new-vtm-v20-game-seeking-additional-roleplayer-writer","id":1450754,"title":"New VtM v20 game seeking additional roleplayer/writer","path":["Home","Onyx Path","General","Conventions, Gatherings, and Online Play"],"posts":[{"date":"2021-06-02T17:48:54-07:00","id":1450754,"title":"New VtM v20 game seeking additional roleplayer/writer","content":"<span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">We are an established group of 5 (GM + 4 players) starting up a new, long-term game of Vampire: The Masquerade (20th anniversary edition).</span><span style=\"font-size:17px\"> We are considering adding a new member to the coterie.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">We have been roleplaying together online for many years.</span><span style=\"font-size:17px\">We have mostly played D&amp;D and Pathfinder, and our last Pathfinder campaign ran continuously 2008-2020 (yes, 12 years!), during the course of which, some of us got married, moved countries, had children, and evolved characters from level 1 to level 19...</span><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Somewhere along the way we got kinda old, too; our ages range from late 30s to early 50s.</span></span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Our games are conducted online via a combination of:</span></span></span><ul><li>Roll20 sessions weekly on Friday or Saturday evenings (CST); and</li> <li>Play-by-post on a private hosted PhPBB forum between sessions.</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">We place a heavy emphasis on roleplaying and character development. With this being an online game, the emphasis on story means it is important that any potential player<b> is comfortable writing descriptively</b>; you don\u2019t need to be Anne Rice, but you do need to enjoy describing your character\u2019s actions, thoughts, appearance, etc, via the written word.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">While we\u2019re very serious about building our collaborative story, we also have a lot of fun, enjoy OOC banter, and laugh a lot. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Our GM is pretty brilliant and really knows how to tell/guide a story.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Player requirements:</span></span></span><ul><li>Focused on character development &amp; roleplaying</li> <li>Able to coherently and descriptively portray your character in writing</li> <li>Friendly, with a good sense of humor</li> <li>No rules lawyers allowed; for balance, we try hard to get the rules \u201cright\u201d (which will take some work for all of us initially in this campaign, as we re-acclimate ourselves to WoD, which has many gray areas) and especially be consistent, but excessive arguing with the GM won\u2019t fly and should never derail a gaming session. We have already identified a number of house rules we will be following, so if you are a VtM purist this may not be your group.</li> <li>Typically has the time &amp; enthusiasm to post on the Roleplay forum several times a week between sessions</li> <li>Is in it for the long haul</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">As mentioned, while we have long played together, this is a brand new campaign (targeted to start in early July), so it's a great opportunity to bring in someone new. Some of us played VtM many years ago, while others are completely new to the system, so consider this fair warning that there will definitely be a learning curve among the group, especially when we get into combat situations.<br /> <br /> The setting will initially be Chicago in 1920 - think prohibition and gangsters - but of course, vampires live a long time, so both location and era are expected to shift over time, especially if this story is as long lived as our last one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Please reply or DM me if interested. This is not first-come/first-served, and if we don't find the right player we will not add anyone. Therefore, if expressing interest, please tell me what you feel comfortable sharing about yourself and, in particular, why you think this is the right fit for you.</span></span></span><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26872-sekhmet","name":"Sekhmet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-03T02:24:36-07:00","id":1450791,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sekhmet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1450754-new-vtm-v20-game-seeking-additional-roleplayer-writer#post1450754\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View