n style=\"font-size:17px\">While we\u2019re very serious about building our collaborative story, we also have a lot of fun, enjoy OOC banter, and laugh a lot. </span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Our GM is pretty brilliant and really knows how to tell/guide a story.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Player requirements:</span></span></span><ul><li>Focused on character development &amp; roleplaying</li> <li>Able to coherently and descriptively portray your character in writing</li> <li>Friendly, with a good sense of humor</li> <li>No rules lawyers allowed; for balance, we try hard to get the rules \u201cright\u201d (which will take some work for all of us initially in this campaign, as we re-acclimate ourselves to WoD, which has many gray areas) and especially be consistent, but excessive arguing with the GM won\u2019t fly and should never derail a gaming session. We have already identified a number of house rules we will be following, so if you are a VtM purist this may not be your group.</li> <li>Typically has the time &amp; enthusiasm to post on the Roleplay forum several times a week between sessions</li> <li>Is in it for the long haul</li> </ul><br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">As mentioned, while we have long played together, this is a brand new campaign (targeted to start in early July), so it's a great opportunity to bring in someone new. Some of us played VtM many years ago, while others are completely new to the system, so consider this fair warning that there will definitely be a learning curve among the group, especially when we get into combat situations.<br /> <br /> The setting will initially be Chicago in 1920 - think prohibition and gangsters - but of course, vampires live a long time, so both location and era are expected to shift over time, especially if this story is as long lived as our last one.</span></span></span><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#000000\"><span style=\"font-family:&amp;quot\"><span style=\"font-size:17px\">Please reply or DM me if interested. This is not first-come/first-served, and if we don't find the right player we will not add anyone. Therefore, if expressing interest, please tell me what you feel comfortable sharing about yourself and, in particular, why you think this is the right fit for you.</span></span></span></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Hello, can you be more precise about when you are playing and for how long? My time zone is very different<br /> <br /> <br /> I am quite intrigued by the game's concept. How realistic will the setting be? (sexism, racism, homophobia, etc) I personally go for total realism, but i can understand why some people would prefer some breaks from reality.<br /> I like this sort of game, because, i love story-driven campaigns/chronicles that are not just a competition about who has a +5 sword of doom lol<br /> I don't mind if the campaign has a learning curve and i like the fact that your group is experienced. (cause rage quitting has derailed quite a few groups)<br /> I do hope that the prohibition against rule-lawyering goes both ways lmao(I always found it annoying when a ST looked me straight in the eye and told me that 2+3 = 6 ,just because a book says so)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1492,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","user":"mark","date":". 06-03-2021, 05:31 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-06T11:02:52-07:00","id":1451148,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>mark</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1450754-new-vtm-v20-game-seeking-additional-roleplayer-writer?p=1450791#post1450791\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hello, can you be more precise about when you are playing and for how long? My time zone is very different<br /> <br /> I am quite intrigued by the game's concept. How realistic will the setting be? (sexism, racism, homophobia, etc) I personally go for total realism, but i can understand why some people would prefer some breaks from reality.<br /> I like this sort of game, because, i love story-driven campaigns/chronicles that are not just a competition about who has a +5 sword of doom lol<br /> I don't mind if the campaign has a learning curve and i like the fact that your group is experienced. (cause rage quitting has derailed quite a few groups)<br /> I do hope that the prohibition against rule-lawyering goes both ways lmao(I always found it annoying when a ST looked me straight in the eye and told me that 2+3 = 6 ,just because a book says so)</div> </div> </div> </div>Hi Mark, We will play primarily on Friday nights but may reschedule to Saturday nights on occasion due to conflicts. We typically begin around 7-8pm and end around 11:00pm CST.<br /> <br /> The setting will be very realistic. The ST is a history buff, actually certified to teach history, and has been reading all about 1920s Chicago lately in preparation (as in, non-fiction books, not just the Vampire source books for Chicago!). Yes, sexism, racism, and homophobia will of course be alive and well in this time period especially. (Of course, a given vampire may or may not share the current cultural views of mortal 1920s America.)<br /> <br /> The ST is very open-minded and will absolutely consider (and solicit) input from others in support of rules interpretations, as needed. But it is important that arguing never derails a session (at least, more than briefly), and players be willing to accept his in-session decision to allow the story to proceed, perhaps with further out-of-session discussions needed to reach a long-term decision on a given rules conundrum. In the end, the ST is of course the final arbiter.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26872-sekhmet","name":"Sekhmet","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar26872_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2021"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2021-06-07T12:55:58-07:00","id":1451245,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sekhmet</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/conventions-and-gatherings/1450754-new-vtm-v20-game-seeking-additional-roleplayer-writer?p=1451148#post1451148\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hi Mark, We will play primarily on Friday nights but may reschedule to Saturday nights on occasion due to conflicts. We typically begin around 7-8pm and end around 11:00pm CST.<br /> <br /> The setting will be very realistic. The ST is a history buff, actually certified to teach history, and has been reading all about 1920s Chicago lately in preparation (as in, non-fiction books, not just the Vampire source books for Chicago!). Yes, sexism, racism, and homophobia will of course be alive and well in this time period especially. (Of course, a given vampire may or may not share the current cultural views of mortal 1920s America.)<br /> <br /> The ST is very open-minded and will absolutely consider (and solicit) input from others in support of rules interpretations, as needed. But it is important that arguing never derails a session (at least, more than briefly), and players be willing to accept his in-session decision to allow the story to proceed, perhaps with further out-of-session discussions needed to reach a long-term decision on a given rules conundrum. In the end, the ST is of course the final arbiter.<br /> <br /> I hope this helps!</div> </div> </div> </div>It sure does. Fun fact, I also got a history degree. <br /> I will check my schedule. I really hope I can make it. Looks like an awesome setting. Do you have a discord channel or something like that.?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1492-mark","name":"mark","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1492_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1379"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}